  "description": "CACGEX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C27 H36 Cl1 Dy3 N3 O13 3+,3(Cl1 1-),C2 H6 O1,C6 H14. From the CIF bond table, Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.526-3.579 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.00-99.21°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [{Dy3(O)2(o-pbd)3Cl(H2O)5}2]·6Cl·2EtOH·2hexane. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
